        "thinking": "Good, wrangler 3.114.17 is available. Now I need to understand what's needed to run this locally. \n\nThe main issues for local dev with `wrangler dev` are:\n1. `HYPERDRIVE` binding - wrangler dev can simulate this with a local connection string via `.dev.vars` or `--var`\n2. R2 bucket - wrangler dev has local R2 simulation\n3. KV namespace - needs an ID, but wrangler dev simulates KV locally\n4. Durable Objects, Queues, Workflows - wrangler dev can simulate these locally\n\n\n5. The `wrangler.toml` has placeholder values like `FILL_IN_AFTER_DEPLOY` for the KV and Hyperdrive IDs, which could cause issues with local development, so I'll need to either create a `.dev.vars` file with the necessary variables or use the `--local` flag with Miniflare to work around these placeholders.\n\n6. KV namespaces work fine locally since wrangler creates local storage automatically, but Hyperdrive is trickier since it's not simulated by Miniflare—I'd need to provide an actual Postgres connection string to test it locally.",
